## The guards

The nose keeps one group of two ids: `l2-w01-practice-line-nose` and `l2-w01-check-row-nose`. A
try of either id counts for the group, so the two ids share the 3 tries of one picture.

The ostrich has the one id `l2-w07-check-row-ostrich`. The id is not in any group, so the
counter counts its own rows. The old olive id and the old week 8 ostrich id left the group.

## The delivery check

`src/storytime/muse-delivery.ts` and its caller can deliver a row only when the picture list
holds that row. The list gives the delivered file names and the pixel size. The approval entry
`fileVersion` already gives the v2 names of a redraw, so that part needed no change.

One gap needed a change. The two D4 prompt rows are named `l2-w05-d4-prompt-face-v1.png` and
`l2-w07-d4-prompt-ball-v1.png`. The row-name pattern `^l2-w\d{2}-[a-z-]+-v\d+\.png$` refused the
digit in the row name, so the delivery stopped before the first write. The pattern now allows a
digit in the row name, and two tests cover the D4 row under the list names and under the v2
names.

The five other new ids (the axe, the ostrich, the moon, the mango, and the drum) sit in the
Workbooks picture list today. The list moved on since the judge kit: SHA-256
`327f805f2f44aeed2b29477e83921ed03cf5fd7ab6600910ca8e21fced5b2cc7`, 194 rows, Workbooks commit
`c618523e`. The judge kit stays frozen and still pins the list v5 SHA-256.

Nothing was written in Workbooks.

