# Step 9 of T4 (the nut attempt 3, 2026-11-05, PM order 08:43 ICT)

role_base_sha: df2aa52e3863dd59641351b60c3950a81358a84e (the strategy commit; also P5R_BASE, test-strategy.md 5.11)
Red model: none (light lane). Green model: kimi-code-plan-cn/kimi-for-coding.

Deviation carried from step 8: this maker replaced the earlier MiniMax maker (session
ses_e5769d3feffe8eIjC22MWAmzDO) at 08:16 ICT.

Why: Workbooks' look at the nut v2 (`l2-w01-story-page-a-nut`, reader "Nan Can Nod" page 5,
sentence "A nut.") found two peanut pods side by side in the color and sparse hatching in the
line art, so a child reads "two nuts" or no nut. The PM wants one peanut in its shell, alone
and large on Nan's palm, a clear shell texture in the line art, and the rest of the page as v2.

## The spec change (commit `6a64a214`)

`docs/storytime/l2-unit1/a48/l2-w01-story-page-a-nut.json`:
- The references now hold the m3 color print as Picture 3. The color prompt uses it for Nan,
  the raised open hand, the pose, the clothes, and the plain white background only, and says
  its nut is wrong (two pods side by side) and must not be copied.
- The color prompt asks for exactly ONE peanut in its shell, alone on the open palm, large
  (about one third of the picture width), in the middle: one single shell, one pod with two
  round bumps joined by one narrow waist, light tan, with a clear netted texture of small
  crossing lines over the whole shell. Not two pods, not two nuts side by side, no other nut,
  no loose kernels.
- The line prompt asks for one single shell with a clear outline of two round bumps and a
  narrow waist, and a dense netted texture of short crossing lines over the whole shell, so it
  reads as a peanut at book size. The other line rules stay.
- `mustShow` is now the four PM phrases.

## The 2 calls (one after the other, no despeckle, no local filter)

| Kind | Command result | Version | Cost (USD) |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| color try 3 | `l2-w01-story-page-a-nut-m4 color ok 1920x1280` | m4 | 0.01 |
| line try 3 | `l2-w01-story-page-a-nut-m4 line try 1 ok 1920x1280` (from `--from 4`) | m4 | 0.01 |

The guard did not refuse either call. The tool prints "line try 1" because its counter keys on
the color version; by the costs.tsv rows this is line try 3 (the m3 line, the m3 line-2, and
the m4 line). Restart spend so far: 0.54 USD of the 1.00 USD cap. These were the LAST color
try and the LAST line try of this picture.

